<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <title>menosketiago™ — Volvo Cars Mobile Design System</title>

    {{> head/meta}}
    {{> head/og}}
    {{> head/links-scripts}}
</head>

<body class="theme-dark">
    <div class="wrapper">
        <header class="work-header">
            {{> layout/work-header}}
        </header>

        <main class="work-main">
            <section class="summary">
                <h1>Volvo Cars Mobile DS</h1>

                <figure>
                    <picture>
                        <source srcset="/images/volvo/splash.avif 1x, /images/volvo/splash-2x.avif 2x"
                            type="image/avif">
                        <source srcset="/images/volvo/splash.webp 1x, /images/volvo/splash-2x.webp 2x"
                            type="image/webp">
                        <img src="/images/volvo/splash.jpg" fetchpriority="high"
                            alt="One the left a hand holding a phone showing the old home tab of the Volvo Cars app, and on the right two hands holding a phone showing the 2026 design">
                    </picture>
                    <figcaption>The old home tab on the Volvo Car app (left) and the new late 2025 design update (right)
                    </figcaption>
                </figure>

                <aside>
                    <div>
                        <h2 class="h-s">Role</h2>

                        <div class="pill-group">
                            <div class="pill">Design System Manager</div>
                            <div class="pill">Staff Product Designer</div>
                            <div class="pill">Product Manager</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h2 class="h-s">Tools</h2>

                        <div class="pill-group row">
                            <div class="pill">JIRA</div>
                            <div class="pill">Figma</div>
                            <div class="pill">FigJam</div>
                            <div class="pill">ProtoPie</div>
                            <div class="pill">JavaScript</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div>
                        <h2 class="h-s">Team</h2>

                        <div class="pill-group row">
                            <div class="pill">Alex Hedin</div>
                            <div class="pill">Malin Czernik</div>
                            <div class="pill">Daniil Gavrilov</div>
                            <div class="pill">Sara Ashour</div>
                            <div class="pill">Martin Delin</div>
                            <div class="pill">Richard Landérus</div>
                            <div class="pill">Richard Jarrett</div>
                            <div class="pill">Fabian Fredholm</div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </aside>

                <article class="grid-2-2">
                    <h3>TLDR summary</h3>

                    <div>
                        <p>
                            From designers asking “Is this component available in iOS?” and engineers complaining about
                            not having the same designs in code as in Figma, to a 100% aligned Design System that made
                            it possible to ship several years of incredible design vision work — stuck inside slide
                            decks — to Volvo owners around the world.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            I fully refactored and evolved our Figma libraries, made sure components and patterns were
                            implemented in collaboration with engineering, and aligned with the overarching Design
                            Tokens architecture, guidelines, and other experience touchpoints like car and web.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Thanks to transparent communication, extensive documentation, and support for 120 designers
                            and engineers, I was able to become the acting Product Manager of a small but mighty team of
                            2 engineers and an Engineering Manager.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Together, we saved roughly 28 million SEK in engineering time and prevented accessibility
                            fines of up to 658 million, while going above WCAG 2.2 AAA level requirements.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </section>

            <h2>Full story</h2>

            <section>
                <article class="grid-2-2">
                    <h3>From WIP to ship</h3>

                    <div>
                        <p>
                            When I started at <b>Volvo Cars</b>, we had old mobile <b>Figma</b> libraries, with outdated
                            color and typography foundations, hard-to-find and overly complex components built without
                            leveraging Figma capabilities like variants and properties, and almost non-existent
                            documentation.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            There were a lot of great insights collected from the design team about their experience
                            with the system, and a work-in-progress library that my colleagues had put together
                            over the previous year.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            After a few days of refactoring, I presented the improvements in a design show-and-tell.
                            There was a lot of excitement from the team, and the Head of Mobile UX asked, "When can you
                            publish this?". My reply was, "Give me 2/3 weeks."
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Two weeks later, I hit publish on a new Mobile Design System library, set the old library to
                            deprecated, and communicated to Designers that they should migrate components in their work
                            progressively to profit from all the improvements.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </section>

            <section>
                <article class="grid-2-2 reverse-order">
                    <h3>Missing alignment</h3>

                    <div>
                        <p>
                            After a few weeks of support requests from designers and engineers, I started noticing a
                            repeating pattern. The components in the code did match the ones in the Figma library, and
                            some were available only on Android or iOS.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            To understand the depth of the problem, I created a Notion database where we could track the
                            alignment status of all components in the system. Out of 35 components in the design
                            library, Android had only 7 fully aligned, and iOS had up to 9.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <figure>
                    <picture loading="lazy">
                        <source srcset="/images/volvo/implementation-tracker.avif" type="image/avif">
                        <source srcset="/images/volvo/implementation-tracker.webp" type="image/webp">
                        <img src="/images/volvo/implementation-tracker.jpg"
                            alt="Screenshot from a Notion table showing different component names and statuses over Figma, Android, and iOS"
                            loading="lazy">
                    </picture>
                    <figcaption class="bottom">The component implementation status tracker (around summer 2025)
                    </figcaption>
                </figure>
            </section>

            <section>
                <article class="grid-2-2">
                    <h3>The devils is in the docs</h3>

                    <div>
                        <p>
                            One of the leading issues found in user research efforts completed before I joined the
                            mobile team was that there was a lack of information about how and when to use components.
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            In fact, the only thing available for each component was a short description present on the
                            component page and the component metadata in Figma (available in the UI panels).
                        </p>
                        <p>
                            Good documentation allows Designers, Engineers, and stakeholders to make sounder decisions
                            and understand the constraints that enable coherent experiences. It's also a great source of
                            context to help LLMs generate designs and prototypes that follow your brand and design
                            language.
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>

                <article class="grid-2-2 reverse-order">
                    <h3>Crafting the context</h3>

                    <div>
                        <p>
                            My first step was creating a getting-started guide that detailed key concepts for utilizing
                            the Design System, with quick start information, but also details on governance, support
                            channels, bug reporting, and more. I also created a changelog where everyone could see
                            additions, changes, and deprecations, and documentation describing how to document
                            components (very meta, I know).
                        </p>
                    </div>
                </article>
            </section>

            {{!-- More work section --}}

            <h2 class="m-th">More work</h2>

            <section class="dual-column">
                {{> summaries/ericsson}}
                {{> summaries/trids}}
            </section>
        </main>

        {{!-- Back to top button --}}
        {{> back-to-top}}

        <footer>
            {{> layout/footer}}
        </footer>
    </div>

    {{> tooltip}}

    <div class="cursor"></div>

    {{!-- JS --}}
    <script src="/index.js" type="text/javascript"></script>
</body>

</html>